      "revision": 1374059903,
      "text": "Ficus ulmifolia is a species of flowering plant in the family Moraceae. It is a tree endemic to the Philippines. it is a small tree, ranging from three to 12 metres tall. It is native to lowland and montane rain forests, where it grows in thickets from 107 to 1,500 meters elevation. It is threatened by habitat loss."
